's branch point\\\\n\\\\n(nothing new)\\\\n\\\\n## this branch's own commits since the branch point\\\\n\\\\n0ef9df110a325e26c701dac4d77af15f759e9b49 attavo driver attavo: verify invocation 01 started for item 194\\\\n77440558501dca2c45689ed44006c790d21f9274 attavo driver attavo: build record for item 194 (build-01)\\\\naa9c02ba125d391f264f1d2facf0da3fa4d87d4e attavo executor (claude-code) attest: sum every invocation's time and cost into the statement (#194)\\\\n4096f8cf673e9d957cf7fbf9ce53824aae536933 attavo driver attavo: build invocation 01 started for item 194\\\\n86d40a84cb9a2636abcd32e2d99f5646f892416f attavo-records[bot] attavo: approval record for item 194\\\\n2c4754587314e481152730e456003a8124d18656 attavo-records[bot] attavo: spec-gate record for item 194\\\\n70d2bc920419432f9f1d66c87e8e2fb4f59d0669 David Bean spec for #194: the first criterion no longer imports jsonschema, which the spec gate's runner does not carry\\\\nd004148ddfefd56e61ac2f12b75fa4f95295dfa2 attavo-records[bot] attavo: spec-gate record for item 194\\\\n9c8f98d6426fb0a431131045127a9e9989a810cb David Bean spec for #194: the statement accounts for the item's time and cost\\\\n\\\\n## markers and records present at 0ef9df110a325e26c701dac4d77af15f759e9b49\\\\n\\\\nattest/records/194/approval-01.json\\\\nattest/records/194/build-01.json\\\\nattest/records/194/build-01.log\\\\nattest/records/194/build-01.started\\\\nattest/records/194/spec-01.json\\\\nattest/records/194/spec-02.json\\\\nattest/records/194/verify-01.started\\\\n\\\\n## check runs for the last three shas on this branch\\\\n\\\\n0ef9df110a325e26c701dac4d77af15f759e9b49: coherence=success, doctor=success, test=success, action-self-check=success, typecheck=success, schema-version=success, spec-gate=success, schema-version=skipped, doctor=skipped, action-self-check=success, test=success, typecheck=success\\\\n77440558501dca2c45689ed44006c790d21f9274: doctor=success, schema-version=success, test=success, action-self-check=success, typecheck=success, coherence=success, spec-gate=success, doctor=skipped, schema-version=skipped, typecheck=success, test=success, action-self-check=success\\\\naa9c02ba125d391f264f1d2facf0da3fa4d87d4e: (no checks)\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nattest/records/194/counsel-01.log:7:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' attest/specs/194/spec.md; sed -n '1,320p' attest/rulings.md; file attest/specs/194/stub; find attest/specs/194/stub -maxdepth 3 -type f -print 2>/dev/null; rg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"'^diff --git|time|cost|AttestRecord|every_attested_item|sealed|statement\\\\\\\" /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp95vzmbhl/diff.patch | head -n 420'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"## Problem\\\\n\\\\nEvery build, verify, and counsel record carries `wall_clock_s` and `cost_usd`, and nothing in the product sums them. The attestation statement carries the final attempt per stage and no more, so a view derived its own figure: on 2026-09-18 the operator screen showed #158 as 20 minutes of product time (its final build plus its final verify, no counsel) where its nineteen invocations ran 114.9 minutes (builds 5,570 s, verifies 909 s, counsels 412 s) against 2,021 minutes of lead time. The item spent six percent of its lead time inside an invocation, which is the number that says where the next minute is worth removing, and no record carried it. The operator ruled 2026-09-19 that this accounting lives in the product; and, the same day, that dollars are summed across stages and executors with a subtotal per executor beside the total (superseding the 2026-09-09 ruling against a cross-executor sum), a total that lacks any record's cost saying so by name. Pricing a record whose executor reports no cost, from a published rate per token shown in Configure, is the cost-basis item and is not this one.\\\\n\\\\nRetires: any view's own arithmetic over records as the source of an item's durations or cost (attavo/screen's Analyze derivation, deleted by a screen item filed against this one); \\\\\\\"product time\\\\\\\" as a name for the final attempt; the statement's silence about every attempt but the last.\\\\n\\\\nThe statement for this item's own merge is printed by the pinned release and carries no `time`; the first statement that does is sealed after the release that ships this and the pin to it. Proof six does not check a statement that carries no `time`.\\\\n\\\\n## Claims\\\\n\\\\n- attavo/attest.py\\\\n- attavo/doctor.py\\\\n- attavo/types.py\\\\n- schema/attestation.schema.json\\\\n- tests/test_attest_time.py\\\\n- tests/test_attest.py\\\\n- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\\\\n\\\\n## Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- attest-sums-every-invocation.sh: on a fixture item with three builds, two verifies, and one counsel, attavo attest prints a statement valid against schema/attestation.schema.json at $id v3 whose time block carries attempts and invocation_s per stage (350.75, 40.0, 7.5), invocation_s 398.25 for the item, lead_s from approval-01's at to the merge's committer time, waiting_s as their difference, and leaves wall_clock_by_stage_s as the final attempt\\\\n- attest-names-a-record-without-wall-clock.sh: when build-02 carries no wall_clock_s, time.not_read is [\\\\\\\"build-02\\\\\\\"], time.build.partial and time.partial are true, time.build.attempts is still 3, and the missing value is never summed as zero\\\\n- attest-sums-cost-across-executors.sh: cost.usd is the sum of every record's cost_usd across stages and adapters with by_stage_usd and by_adapter_usd beside it; while one adapter's records carry no cost the total is partial and not_read names each such record; once they carry one the total is whole and both adapters have a subtotal\\\\n- doctor-fails-a-statement-whose-time-is-not-its-records.sh: proof every-attested-item-is-sealed holds on a sealed statement whose time.invocation_s equals its records' sum, fails naming item 1 and time.invocation_s when the statement says 20.0, and holds on a statement sealed before time existed\\\\n- the-accounting-has-its-tests.sh: tests/test_attest_time.py carries the four regression tests by name, attavo/types.py's AttestRecord mirrors the schema's properties, and the schema requires time and cost\\\\n# Rulings\\\\n\\\\nWritten by the merge of a proposed amendment only.\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub: directory\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub/tests/test_attest_time.py\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub/schema/attestation.schema.json\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub/attavo/types.py\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub/attavo/attest.py\\\\nattest/specs/194/stub/attavo/doctor.py\\\\n1:diff --git a/attavo/attest.py b/attavo/attest.py\\\\n9:+from datetime import datetime\\\\n16:-from attavo.types import ApprovalRecord, AttestRecord, BuildRecord, SpecRecord, VerifyRecord\\\\n17:+from attavo.types import (ApprovalRecord, AttestRecord, BuildRecord, ItemCost, ItemTime,\\\\n33:+def item_time_and_cost(records_dir: Path, sealed_at_epoch: int | None) -> tuple[ItemTime, ItemCost]:\\\\n37:+    and counsel attempt's wall_clock_s and cost_usd, per stage and for the\\\\n41:+    `at` to sealed_at_epoch (the committer time of the commit the statement\\\\n44:+    records and fails a sealed statement whose invocation_s disagrees.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n46:+    time_not_read: list[str] = []\\\\n47:+    cost_not_read: list[str] = []\\\\n61:+                time_not_read.append(name)\\\\n62:+            cost = rec.get(\\\\\\\"cost_usd\\\\\\\")\\\\n63:+            if _is_number(cost):\\\\n64:+                by_stage[stage] = by_stage.get(stage, 0.0) + float(cost)\\\\n67:+                by_adapter[key] = by_adapter.get(key, 0.0) + float(cost)\\\\n69:+                cost_not_read.append(name)\\\\n76:+    if first_approval and sealed_at_epoch is not None:\\\\n79:+            approved = datetime.fromisoformat(str(at).replace(\\\\\\\"Z\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"+00:00\\\\\\\"))\\\\n80:+            lead_s = round(sealed_at_epoch - approved.timestamp(), 3)\\\\n82:+            time_not_read.append(f\\\\\\\"approval-{min(first_approval):02d}\\\\\\\")\\\\n83:+    item_time: ItemTime = {\\\\n89:+        \\\\\\\"not_read\\\\\\\": time_not_read,\\\\n91:+    item_cost: ItemCost = {\\\\n95:+        \\\\\\\"partial\\\\\\\": bool(cost_not_read),\\\\n96:+        \\\\\\\"not_read\\\\\\\": cost_not_read,\\\\n98:+    return item_time, item_cost\\\\n109:+        sealed_at: int | None = int(git(root, \\\\\\\"show\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"-s\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--format=%ct\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\").strip())\\\\n110:+    except (RuntimeError, ValueError):\\\\n111:+        sealed_at = None\\\\n112:+    item_time, item_cost = item_time_and_cost(records_dir, sealed_at)\\\\n114:     statement: AttestRecord = {\\\\n121:-        # across vendors: a stage's executor may report no cost at all.\\\\n122:+        # The final attempt per stage; every attempt, summed, is in `time`\\\\n123:+        # and `cost` (the sum across executors was ruled 2026-09-19).\\\\n124:         \\\\\\\"cost_by_stage_usd\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"build\\\\\\\": latest_build.get(\\\\\\\"cost_usd\\\\\\\"), \\\\\\\"verify\\\\\\\": latest_verify.get(\\\\\\\"cost_usd\\\\\\\")},\\\\n127:+        \\\\\\\"time\\\\\\\": item_time,\\\\n128:+        \\\\\\\"cost\\\\\\\": item_cost,\\\\n132:diff --git a/attavo/doctor.py b/attavo/doctor.py\\\\n141:+from attavo.attest import check_attest_chain, item_time_and_cost\\\\n149:+def _time_disagrees(item_records_dir: Path, item: str, merge_sha: str,\\\\n150:+                    statement: dict[str, Any]) -> str | None:\\\\n151:+    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"A sealed statement that carries `time` says the invocation_s its\\\\n153:+    same records (no record is written after a merge). A statement sealed\\\\n154:+    before `time` existed carries none and is not checked. No new read of\\\\n155:+    the store: the statement is the one proof six already holds.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n156:+    inner = statement.get(\\\\\\\"predicate\\\\\\\")\\\\n157:+    predicate = inner if isinstance(inner, dict) else statement\\\\n158:+    stated_time = predicate.get(\\\\\\\"time\\\\\\\")\\\\n159:+    if not isinstance(stated_time, dict):\\\\n161:+    summed = item_time_and_cost(item_records_dir, None)[0][\\\\\\\"invocation_s\\\\\\\"]\\\\n162:+    stated = stated_time.get(\\\\\\\"invocation_s\\\\\\\")\\\\n164:+        return (f\\\\\\\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: the statement's time.invocation_s \\\\\\\"\\\\n169: def proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) -> Proof:\\\\n170:     p = Proof(\\\\\\\"every-attested-item-is-sealed\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"every attested item has its statement in the store\\\\\\\")\\\\n172:@@ -646,6 +666,9 @@ def proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) ->\\\\n173:         statement, exit_code = statement_for(root, cmd, merge_sha)\\\\n174:         if statement is not None:\\\\n175:             sealed.append(item)\\\\n176:+            disagreement = _time_disagrees(records_dir / item, item, merge_sha, statement)\\\\n182:diff --git a/attavo/types.py b/attavo/types.py\\\\n191:+    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"One stage's invocations summed (the statement's `time` block).\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n199:+    the item's lead time -- summed from the records by `attavo attest`, so\\\\n212:+    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Every record's cost_usd summed: the item's total across stages and\\\\n214:+    cost_usd is named in not_read and makes every sum it belongs to\\\\n223: class AttestRecord(TypedDict):\\\\n224:     \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The statement `attavo attest` prints (schema/attestation.schema.json).\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n226:@@ -161,6 +194,8 @@ class AttestRecord(TypedDict):\\\\n228:     cost_by_stage_usd: dict[str, float | None]\\\\n230:+    time: ItemTime\\\\n231:+    cost: ItemCost\\\\n235:diff --git a/attest/records/194/approval-