ed statement to its records (#204). Its review found two ways a false statement still holds: a statement carrying `\\\"time\\\": null` and no `cost` is read as sealed before the accounting existed, because absence is tested by value and not by key, and is not checked at all; and both sides of every number are converted to float before they are compared, so an integer one past 2**53 equals the float beside it, where the spec says exactly. No sealed statement carries these fields until the release after this one, so the fixes land before any immutable statement can meet the defects.\\n\\nEvery review record carries `weak_stub`, `stub_ratio`, and `mutation`, and `attavo verify` writes false, null, and null at both of its write sites: three measurements no release has computed. They said \\\"fine\\\" on #194 and #204, where the build shipped the spec author's stub almost line for line and the review judged that author's code without knowing it; on #206, the first item with a thin stub, the review found nothing wrong with the code. `stub_ratio` becomes real: the share of the lines the item's diff adds, outside the specs and records directories and blank lines aside, that are a line of the stub's file at the same path. `weak_stub` and `mutation` are deleted until something earns them; the review record's schema moves to version 6.\\n\\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin by the operator's ruling of 2026-09-20: its `stub_ratio` answers 0.0 without reading the diff and it does not touch `attavo/doctor.py`, so six of the eight tests named below fail on it. The two proof-six fixes have no criterion of their own; the required `test` check runs the two tests the review named, and the second criterion keeps them from being dropped. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the built tree with no `type: ignore`; the builder runs it last, after its final change to any file.\\n\\nRetires: `weak_stub`; `mutation`; `stub_ratio` as a constant; the float conversion in `_same`; absence tested by value.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- attavo/doctor.py\\n- attavo/verify.py\\n- attavo/types.py\\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n- tests/test_stub_ratio.py\\n- tests/test_attest_time.py\\n- tests/test_file_findings.py\\n- tests/test_verify.py\\n- adapters/claude-code/run\\n- adapters/codex/run\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- verify-records-a-stub-ratio-and-drops-two-fields.sh: on a fixture item built and reviewed on its own branch, verify-01 passes and carries stub_ratio as a number from 0 to 1 and neither weak_stub nor mutation; schema/records/verify.schema.json is at version 6, requires and describes stub_ratio, and declares neither of the other two\\n- the-pre-release-fixes-have-their-tests.sh: tests/test_attest_time.py carries the two tests #204's review named, tests/test_stub_ratio.py carries its six by name, and neither attavo/verify.py, attavo/types.py, nor the review record's schema names weak_stub or mutation\\n=== criteria/the-pre-release-fixes-have-their-tests.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\nfor t in test_doctor_rejects_null_time_without_cost test_doctor_rejects_large_integer_that_rounds_to_summed_float\\ndo\\n  grep -q \\\"^def $t(\\\" tests/test_attest_time.py\\ndone\\nfor t in test_stub_ratio_is_one_when_every_added_line_is_the_stubs test_stub_ratio_is_the_share_across_files_and_ignores_blank_lines test_stub_ratio_matches_a_line_only_against_the_stubs_file_at_the_same_path test_stub_ratio_does_not_count_the_specs_or_the_records_directory test_stub_ratio_is_null_with_no_stub_or_no_added_line_and_never_zero test_verify_records_the_ratio_and_no_longer_carries_the_two_fields_nothing_computed\\ndo\\n  grep -q \\\"^def $t(\\\" tests/test_stub_ratio.py\\ndone\\n! grep -rqE 'weak_stub|\\\"mutation\\\"' attavo/verify.py attavo/types.py schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n=== criteria/verify-records-a-stub-ratio-and-drops-two-fields.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d \\\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/attavo.XXXXXX\\\")\\ncp -R \\\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/.\\\" \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ncd \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email fixture@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"fixture\\\"\\nprintf '\\\\n[forge]\\\\nchecks_command = \\\"printf '\\\"'\\\"'ci success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\"'\\\"'\\\"\\\\n' >> attavo.toml\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -q -m install\\ngit init -q --bare -b main \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit remote add origin \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit push -q origin HEAD:main 2>/dev/null\\ngit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\ngit symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD refs/remotes/origin/main\\ngit checkout -q -b attavo/1-x\\nA=\\\"python3 $here/bin/attavo\\\"\\n$A spec-gate 1 >/dev/null\\n$A approve 1 --by alice >/dev/null\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null 2>&1\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null 2>&1\\npython3 - \\\"$here\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(\\\"records/1/verify-01.json\\\"))\\nassert r[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"pass\\\", r[\\\"status\\\"]\\nratio = r[\\\"stub_ratio\\\"]\\nassert isinstance(ratio, (int, float)) and not isinstance(ratio, bool) and 0 <= ratio <= 1, ratio\\nassert \\\"weak_stub\\\" not in r and \\\"mutation\\\" not in r, sorted(r)\\ns = json.load(open(sys.argv[1] + \\\"/schema/records/verify.schema.json\\\"))\\nassert s[\\\"$id\\\"].endswith(\\\"/verify/6\\\"), s[\\\"$id\\\"]\\nassert \\\"weak_stub\\\" not in s[\\\"properties\\\"] and \\\"mutation\\\" not in s[\\\"properties\\\"], sorted(s[\\\"properties\\\"])\\nassert \\\"stub_ratio\\\" in s[\\\"required\\\"] and s[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"stub_ratio\\\"].get(\\\"description\\\"), s[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"stub_ratio\\\"]\\nPY\\ncd \\\"$here\\\"\\nrm -rf \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n      78 stub/tests/test_stub_ratio.py\\n     281 stub/tests/test_attest_time.py\\n      92 stub/tests/test_file_findings.py\\n     222 stub/attavo/types.py\\n     334 stub/attavo/verify.py\\n     119 stub/schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n    1126 total\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ddda